    {
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Why a settled distance stays fixed",
      "level": 1,
      "sources": [
        "lecture-02"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Take the vertex \\(u\\) with the smallest tentative distance.",
        "Any other path to it leaves the settled set through a vertex whose tentative distance is at least that large.",
        "Non-negative weights can only add to that, so no later path is shorter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tone": "pitfall",
      "sources": [
        "lecture-02"
